        <div class="about-grid" data-r>
            <div>
                <p>I have spent six years on mobile, almost all of it on Android, and the last two moving
                    teams onto shared codebases with <strong>Kotlin Multiplatform</strong>. I like the problems
                    that sit underneath a feature — how state is owned, what happens on a cold start, what a
                    request does when the network is hostile.</p>
                <p>Most of my recent work is AI-adjacent consumer product: a live translator, a keyboard, a
                    photo upscaler. They share a shape — a thin native seam over a shared core, a metered
                    backend, and store policy on both sides. I have shipped that shape four times now, and the
                    second one went considerably better than the first.</p>
                <p>I currently lead the mobile team at <strong>Envobyte Ltd.</strong>, where I oversee
                    architecture, code reviews, feature development, and release coordination. I
                    care about <strong>tests around the parts that are hard to reason about</strong>, honest
                    estimates, and leaving a codebase easier to join than I found it.</p>
                <p>Right now I am open to senior Android and Kotlin Multiplatform roles, remote or based in
                    Bangladesh.</p>
